  "summary": "This study compares a pristine Ti3C2Tx control, an electrode-engineered MXene/CPAQ film, and a fabricated rGO/RuO2 positive reference electrode used in asymmetric devices. MXene/CPAQ was prepared by integrating in situ PAQ carbonization, KOH treatment, and PMMA-template sacrificing, producing increased surface =O sites, larger spacing, and higher SSA. The headline MXene/CPAQ electrode achieved 788.4 F g\u22121 at 2 mV s\u22121 in 3 m H2SO4 + 50 mm CuSO4 + 70 mm VOSO4. No electrode thicknesses, mass loadings, flake sizes, pore averages, or volumetric/areal capacitances were reported in the supplied text."
